        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='width:100%;height:100%;overflow:auto;box-sizing:border-box;container-type:inline-size;background:#ffffff;font-family:Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#0f172a'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5cqw,40px) 64px'><div style='padding-top:32px'><header data-role='masthead'><div style='padding:10px 0;border-top:3px solid #0f172a;border-bottom:1px solid #0f172a;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>TWILITE ZONE · CONTRACT</div><h1 style='margin:40px 0 0;font:500 clamp(40px,9.5cqw,72px)/.98 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.025em;text-wrap:balance;color:#0f172a'>Gesture ownership</h1><p style='margin:18px 0 0;max-width:36ch;font:italic 400 clamp(20px,3.6cqw,26px)/1.35 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#475569'>Every press, drag and turn of the wheel on the canvas has one owner, chosen once, by what was touched. How a thing looks changes with zoom; who owns a gesture does not.</p></header></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>One law across every renderer</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><span style='float:left;padding:6px 10px 0 0;font:500 68px/54px Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#0f172a'>T</span>he host classifies the target of a gesture before any renderer acts. Mouse, pointer, touch and wheel input use the same words: the target is one of resize handle, connection handle, control, portal or link, editable content, edge, scroll region, embedded frame, node body, workspace tile or canvas, and each has one owner. Native nodes, authored HTML, Portals and Methods adapt to this; none of them invents its own rule for who gets a press (<code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/NodeGraph/interactionArbiter.js</code>).</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Who owns a press</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>The first of these that applies owns it:</p><ol style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:26px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A resize handle resizes.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A connection handle (a Port&#39;s handle) starts a connection.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A control (a button, an input, a select, anything a surface declares as a control) is activated.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A Portal or a link navigates.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Editable content is edited.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A scroll region scrolls.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>An edge is selected.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>An embedded frame keeps the press, unless its surface says it is canvas-first, when the press goes to the canvas.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A node&#39;s body drags the node. If the node is pinned, the press goes to the canvas and pans the view.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A workspace tile is selected.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Empty canvas pans the view.</li></ol><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Selecting is a deliberate act, never a side effect of dragging.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>The wheel</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>A scroll region owns the wheel while it can scroll in the direction asked. Once it cannot, the wheel goes back to the canvas and zooms. An embedded frame owns the wheel unless its surface is canvas-first.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Pinned nodes</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Pinning changes only who owns a press on a node&#39;s body. A press on the body of a pinned node pans the canvas, even where that body holds or scrolls content. Nothing about a pinned node is dead: its controls, links, fields, scrollbars and frames still answer, and it is moved by its title bar, where its buttons are still buttons.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>What a node&#39;s content answers</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>A node&#39;s content is its face. A click on it is a click on the node, and brings you a step closer to it (the navigation scheme&#39;s node ladder). The content answers on its own in two cases only: what was pressed is something a person operates (a link, a button, a field), or you are inside the node.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Zoom chooses views, not rules</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Glyph, icon, summary, detail and the other bands choose what is drawn. They do not change who owns a gesture. Each surface says whether it is content-first, where the controls, links, scrolling and editing it declares answer, or canvas-first, where every other press is the canvas&#39;s.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>A renderer must not patch the rule</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>The law has failed when a renderer repairs itself with a private <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>stopPropagation</code>, <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>pointer-events</code> or frame exception that changes how another surface behaves. A press that is classified wrongly is fixed in the shared classification (<code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>classifyGestureTarget</code>), not hidden in the renderer that noticed it.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Evidence</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/interactionArbiter.test.js</code> holds the precedence, the wheel rule, the pinned-body rule, the title bar and the workspace tile. <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/NodeGraph/interactionArbiter.js</code> is the one place the order is written.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:40px'><div style='display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:stretch;gap:28px 32px'><div style='flex:1 1 190px;min-width:0'><section data-role='route' data-prominence='secondary' style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #0f172a'><h2 style='margin:0 0 8px;font:500 22px/1.1 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#0f172a'>Contracts</h2><p style='margin:0 0 10px;font:400 14px/1.55 system-ui;color:#475569'>The contracts that use the current vocabulary.</p><a data-role='route-link' href='tlz://twilite.zone/library/documentation/contracts/root.node' style='margin-top:auto;font:700 13px/20px system-ui;text-decoration:none;color:#475569'>Open the contracts →</a></section></div></div></div></div></div>"
        },
        "memo": "",
        "link": ""
      }
    },
